  "question": {
    "text": "Given the electric field of a complete amplitude modulated wave as\n$$\n\\vec{E}=\\hat{i} E_c\\left(1+\\frac{E_m}{E_c} \\cos \\omega_m t\\right) \\cos \\omega_c t\n$$\nWhere the subscript c stands for the carrier wave and $\\mathrm{m}$ for the modulating signal. The frequencies present in the modulated wave are",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AeRuj",
      "text": "\n$\\omega_c$ and $\\sqrt{\\omega_c^2+\\omega_m^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SjcDx",
      "text": "\n$\\omega_c, \\omega_c+\\omega_m$ and $\\omega_c-\\omega_m$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "lWEHH",
      "text": "\n$\\omega_c$ and $\\omega_m$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Em6Z2",
      "text": "\n$\\omega_c$ and $\\sqrt{\\omega_c \\omega_m}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The frequencies present in amplitude modulated wave are :\nCarrier frequency $=\\omega_c$\nUpper side band frequency $=\\omega_c+\\omega_m$\nLower side band frequency $=\\omega_c-\\omega_m$.",
